From: PS4 port
Subject: [PATCH] orbis: resolve the GL entry points from the hardware-render callback

A .prx has its own symbol table and no dynamic linker, so the GLES core ABI a core calls directly
- glTexImage2D, glTexParameteri, glRenderbufferStorageMultisample here - arrives at the link as
plain undefined symbols. ps4/orbis_gl_forward.c answers them with thunks that jump to the
frontend's implementations, and those are null until something hands them a proc-address function.

Most GL cores go through libretro-common's glsm, and orbis_gl_forward.c took the function from it.
Play! does not use glsm at all - it keeps its own retro_hw_render_callback - so the thunk table
stayed empty. The frontend gives get_proc_address to EVERY hardware-rendered core in that
callback, so this passes it straight in, at the first moment there is a context to ask.

diff --git a/Source/ui_libretro/main_libretro.cpp b/Source/ui_libretro/main_libretro.cpp
index 8a07c26..c7c03a3 100644
--- a/Source/ui_libretro/main_libretro.cpp
+++ b/Source/ui_libretro/main_libretro.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,14 @@ retro_input_state_t g_input_state_cb;
 retro_audio_sample_batch_t g_set_audio_sample_batch_cb;
 
 std::map<int, int> g_ds2_to_retro_btn_map;
+#ifdef __ORBIS__
+extern "C" {
+typedef void (*orbis_gl_proc_t)(void);
+typedef orbis_gl_proc_t (*orbis_gl_getproc_t)(const char *sym);
+int orbis_gl_resolve_proc(orbis_gl_getproc_t getproc);
+}
+#endif
+
 struct retro_hw_render_callback g_hw_render
 {
 };
@@ -99,6 +107,14 @@ static void retro_context_reset()
 {
 	CLog::GetInstance().Print(LOG_NAME, "%s\n", __FUNCTION__);
 
+#ifdef __ORBIS__
+	// A .prx carries its own symbol table and has no dynamic linker to ask, so the GLES core ABI
+	// this core calls directly - glTexImage2D and the rest - arrives as undefined symbols and is
+	// satisfied by thunks in ps4/orbis_gl_forward.c. They are null until something hands them the
+	// frontend's proc-address function, and this is the first moment there is a context to ask.
+	orbis_gl_resolve_proc(reinterpret_cast<orbis_gl_getproc_t>(g_hw_render.get_proc_address));
+#endif
+
 	if(m_virtualMachine)
 	{
 		SetupVideoHandler();
